431	% the pairwise-agreement hypothesis over every pair (x, y_1), including pairs carrying
432	% probability zero under D, on which no conditional distribution of y_2 is defined; the
433	% hypothesis is restated here over the pairs of positive marginal probability, the only
434	% pairs the sampling in the hypothesis can refer to and the only ones the averaged
435	% conclusion depends on. The NEEXP original (references/neexp-paper/
